# X : emit the push of a word's or an atom's runtime address.
#
# This is the body of the ′ case, lifted out into a word because M-CHAIN2's
# chain definitions need the same thing three times over: "push the address of
# the thing named by this byte".  A defined word has a body to point at.  An
# ATOM does not — it is a template in the blob, not callable code — so its
# template is wrapped in a thunk [prologue][template][epilogue], emitted inline
# and jumped over, and the thunk's address is pushed instead.  That is what
# makes ′+ and a chain link like ÷ work without the user wrapping anything.
# A name that is neither may be a word defined further down (M2 for long names,
# W10-A for one-byte ones): push a forward thunk, patched by its definition.  If
# it never comes (`′typo`) it is rejected exactly as a plain call to it would
# be — `GOLF: undefined word <name>`, exit 2, at end of input (W9-1C, W10-A).

:X          # X : emit `push <the address of the word or atom named b>` [ b -> ]
→b
←b
Y
@           # dict[name]: a defined word's body address, or 0
"
[           # 0 -> not a word (yet), so an atom or a word defined further down:
_
←b
f
?           #   its blob record's key byte, 0 for the sentinel — always, for
[           #   a long name.  Not an atom: a word defined further down (M2,
233o        #   W10-A).  Its address is not known yet, so push a thunk that jumps to
5w          #   it instead: jmp over [jmp rel32], with that rel32 on the name's
←p          #   pending list.  ⍎ calling the thunk lands in the word through a
→r          #   tail jump, so it behaves exactly like the word itself.
233
‹forward›
L
←r
606208﹣
w
^
]
233o        #   an atom: 0xE9 = jmp over the thunk, around its own template
←p
→j          #   the jmp's placeholder site
0
w
←p
→r          #   the thunk itself starts here
1E          #   [prologue]
←b
E           #   [the atom's own template]
94E         #   [epilogue]
←j
k           #   backpatch the jmp to land after the thunk
L
←r
606208-
w           #   emit `push imm32 <the thunk's address>`
^
]
606208-      # a defined word: push its body address directly
L
w
;


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Locals (M-FRAME, sized per definition since M-FRAME2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A ⊡ word's locals are NAMES — `a`…`h` or any ‹long name› — and each gets the
# next slot at its first appearance in the definition, so a word that names k
# locals has a frame of exactly k cells: slot i at [rbp+8*i], the return address
# at [rbp+8*k].  The slot is known the moment the name is read, so ⇒/⇐ stay
# five fixed bytes; only k is not known until `;`, and that is the frame-size
# immediate's problem (see ⊡, `^` and `;` in `t`).  At most 16 locals, which
# keeps every displacement a disp8 (8*15 = 120 < 128).

:‹badlocal› # ‹badlocal› : reject the local named b      [ msgblock -> !!! ]
←b
256<
1﹢
[           # a one-byte name: V shows the byte, as M-FRAME always did
V
]
←b          # a long name: ‹die› shows it in full
64﹡
4702208﹢
‹die›
;

:‹slot›     # ‹slot› : the rbp displacement of the local named b [ -> disp ]
←b
256<
1﹢
[           # a one-byte local is a..h, as it always was.  ⇒z or ⇒A is
←b          #   refused rather than quietly given a slot: a one-letter local
97﹣         #   is still a deliberate, small namespace
8<
[
“GOLF: local out of range “
‹badlocal›
]
]
←J
[           # OUTSIDE a ⊡ word there is no table: today's fixed a..h slot,
←b          #   name - 'a', exactly as M-FRAME compiled it
256<
[           #   and a long name has nowhere to go at all
“GOLF: local out of range “
‹badlocal›
]
←b
97﹣
8﹡
^
]
0
→‹idx›
{           # this definition's slot table, in order of first appearance
←‹idx›
←‹locals›
﹣
[           #   not named yet: claim the next slot
←‹locals›
16<
[           #     a 17th local would need a disp32: refuse it
“GOLF: too many locals “
‹badlocal›
]
←b
←‹locals›
4﹡
4259936﹢
!           #     slot table[k] = b
←‹locals›
"
1﹢
→‹locals›
8﹡          #     displacement 8*k
^
]
←‹idx›
4﹡
4259936﹢
@
←b
